{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1138398-lore-of-the-beast-demon-the-fallen","id":1138398,"title":"Lore of the Beast (Demon The Fallen)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-07T14:19:04-07:00","id":1138398,"title":"Lore of the Beast (Demon The Fallen)","content":"<b>* Summon Animals</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This evocations allows the Devourer to detect the presence of animals in the surrounding area and to summon those creatures to his side. Those animals instinctively protect the demon. </span></span><br /> <b>System:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Roll Perception + Animal Ken. If your roll is successful, your character get's a detailed sense of the varied animal life in her area, from insects to mammals. The Devourer's awareness extends in a radius of miles equal to her faith score. Armed with this knowledge, the Devourer can chose which animals of a single type she wishes to summon, up to the number of successes rolled. If the Devourer wishes to summon a swarm of vermin or insects, instead the number of successes rolled determines the number of square yards that the swarm covers. These animals flock to the Devourer's side as quickly as possible and circle her protectively, attacking anyone who threatens. The effects of this evocation last for the duration of the scene or until the demon frees the animals. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Suppose i made a roll and managed to summon about 3 Large individual dogs, but i want more. i think it'd be unfair to keep rolling until i've like an army of dogs, that also trumps the point of having increased Animal Ken and Perception or having anything that improves or adds to those two traits. So do i settle for the number i have? can i release the current animals and make a new summoning attempt to see if the numbers fit my expectations? Can i summon 2 species seperately? like summon large dogs and then have some birds around aswell? If i attack a target with my animals, does he get the multiple opponents difficulty aswell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T04:37:55-07:00","id":1138550,"title":"","content":"Anyone answers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T04:51:40-07:00","id":1138551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>onedayumay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1138398-lore-of-the-beast-demon-the-fallen#post1138398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>* Summon Animals</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This evocations allows the Devourer to detect the presence of animals in the surrounding area and to summon those creatures to his side. Those animals instinctively protect the demon. </span></span><br /> <b>System:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Roll Perception + Animal Ken. If your roll is successful, your character get's a detailed sense of the varied animal life in her area, from insects to mammals. The Devourer's awareness extends in a radius of miles equal to her faith score. Armed with this knowledge, the Devourer can chose which animals of a single type she wishes to summon, up to the number of successes rolled. If the Devourer wishes to summon a swarm of vermin or insects, instead the number of successes rolled determines the number of square yards that the swarm covers. These animals flock to the Devourer's side as quickly as possible and circle her protectively, attacking anyone who threatens. The effects of this evocation last for the duration of the scene or until the demon frees the animals. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Suppose i made a roll and managed to summon about 3 Large individual dogs, but i want more. i think it'd be unfair to keep rolling until i've like an army of dogs, that also trumps the point of having increased Animal Ken and Perception or having anything that improves or adds to those two traits. So do i settle for the number i have? can i release the current animals and make a new summoning attempt to see if the numbers fit my expectations? Can i summon 2 species seperately? like summon large dogs and then have some birds around aswell? If i attack a target with my animals, does he get the multiple opponents difficulty aswell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could be wrong, but I suspect you can just keep spamming it for more animals and different species. If you want a rule to go with it, may be you keep your Faith Score number of last summons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T06:48:12-07:00","id":1138565,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's how I see it too. You want to have more Animal Ken and Perception to not Botch, and to use them for other things. If you keep rolling endlessly you will Botch and/or start employing the Tormented version by accident, which may not be what you want. Also the animals need to get there by their own means (chained dogs, or dogs that are indoors may be unable to come), and the power isn't eternal. I don't think it's OP when compared with other Lores.<br /> <br /> And about the multiple opponents difficulty, I think &quot;swarm rules&quot; should start to apply sooner or latter (like a swarm of insects), you don't apply &quot;the multiple opponents difficulty&quot; to 100 bees. That rule it's not balanced for such encounters, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-08-2017, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}